Not accidental.
Not fleeting.

Chōbei squeezes his hand once.
Grounding.

“Then don’t,” he says.
Simple.
Certain.

The tension in Tsukihiko’s chest loosens—just a little.
Enough to breathe.

“…You’re not bothered,” Tsukihiko says after a moment.

