Stay that way.

“You’re still shaking,” Chōbei murmurs.

“I’m not.”

“Mm.”

A beat.
Then—
Chōbei’s free hand comes up, light, careful, brushing a stray piece of hair away from Tsukihiko’s face.
Not rushed.
Not teasing.
Just… gentle.

Tsukihiko stills completely.

“…You’re doing that on purpose,” he says quietly.

